\begin{slide}
Alternatives to Weighting: Decentralized Filtering
\begin{itemize}
  \item Decentralized filtering without feedback
  \item Decentralized filtering with feedback
\end{itemize} 
\end{slide}

\begin{slide}
Decentralized Filtering without Feedback
\begin{itemize}
  \item Assume two local filters (like CT I)
  \item Then for the global error covariance we have:
\[P^{-1}=P_1^{-1}+M_1^{-1}+P_2^{-1}+M_2^{-1}+M^{-1}\]
where $P_1,P_2$ are updated local error covariances for each filter, $M_1,M_2$ are extrapolated local error covariances prior to update, and $M$ is the global filter's prior error covariance.
\end{itemize} 
\end{slide}

\begin{slide}
Decentralized Filtering without Feedback
\begin{itemize}
  \item The global filter's estimate is
\[\hat{x}=P\left[P_1^{-1}\hat{x}_1-M_1m_1^{-1}+P_1^{-1}\hat{x}_2-M_2m_1^{-1}\right]\]
\end{itemize} 
\end{slide}
